# Tool Input Validation

| Field  | Value                |
| ------ | -------------------- |
| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | In Progress          |

Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.

## Validation at execute time

- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L6), [validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input with undeclared properties through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L54)).
- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake.

## Schema compilation and caching

- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: compiles a static schema once across ten executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L17)).
- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: validates each function-valued definition against its current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L30)).

## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery

- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns schema rejections to the provider so it can correct a tool call](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L401), [validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
import type {ToolDefinition} from '../../types/ai.js';
import Ajv, {type ValidateFunction} from 'ajv';
import type {OutgoingMessage} from '../../types/messages.js';
import {log} from '../../shared/logger.js';

export interface ToolResponse {
  result: string;
  clientMessages?: OutgoingMessage[];
  suppressAssistantResponse?: boolean;
}

export interface ToolContext {
  userId: string | number;
  sessionId?: string;
  workspaceId?: string | number;
  authHeaders?: {
    cookie?: string;
    authorization?: string;
    host?: string;
  };
}

export type ToolExecutor = (input: Record<string, unknown>, context?: ToolContext) => Promise<string | ToolResponse>;

export function normalizeToolResponse(response: string | ToolResponse): ToolResponse {
  return typeof response === 'string' ? {result: response} : response;
}

export type ToolDefinitionSource = ToolDefinition | (() => ToolDefinition);

function decodeJsonPointerPart(part: string): string {
  return part.replace(/~1/g, '/').replace(/~0/g, '~');
}

function isRequiredError(keyword: string): boolean {
  return keyword === 'required';
}

function resolveInstancePath(instancePath: string, dataPath: string | undefined, schemaProperties: string[]): string {
  if (instancePath) return instancePath;
  const normalizedDataPath = normalizeDataPath(dataPath);
  if (normalizedDataPath) return normalizedDataPath;
  return schemaProperties.join('/');
}

function normalizeDataPath(dataPath?: string): string | undefined {
  if (!dataPath) return undefined;
  return dataPath.replace(/\.([a-zA-Z0-9_$-]+)/g, '/$1').replace(/^\//, '');
}

export interface RegisteredTool {
  definition: ToolDefinition;
  execute: ToolExecutor;
}

interface StoredTool {
  definitionSource: ToolDefinitionSource;
  execute: ToolExecutor;
}

export class ToolRegistry {
  private readonly tools = new Map<string, StoredTool>();
  private readonly validators = new WeakMap<object, ValidateFunction>();
  private readonly ajv = new Ajv({
    strict: false,
    validateFormats: false,
    allErrors: true,
  } as unknown as ConstructorParameters<typeof Ajv>[0]);

  private compile(definition: ToolDefinition): ValidateFunction {
    const schema = definition.inputSchema;
    const cached = this.validators.get(schema);
    if (cached) return cached;
    try {
      const validate = this.ajv.compile(schema);
      this.validators.set(schema, validate);
      return validate;
    } catch (error) {
      throw new Error(`Invalid input schema for tool ${definition.name}: ${String(error)}`, {cause: error});
    }
  }

  private resolveDefinition(source: ToolDefinitionSource): ToolDefinition {
    return typeof source === 'function' ? source() : source;
  }

  register(definition: ToolDefinitionSource, execute: ToolExecutor): void {
    const resolved = this.resolveDefinition(definition);
    if (typeof definition !== 'function') this.compile(resolved);
    this.tools.set(resolved.name, {definitionSource: definition, execute});
  }

  get(name: string): RegisteredTool | undefined {
    const tool = this.tools.get(name);
    if (!tool) return undefined;
    return {definition: this.resolveDefinition(tool.definitionSource), execute: tool.execute};
  }

  getDefinitions(): ToolDefinition[] {
    return [...this.tools.values()].map(t => this.resolveDefinition(t.definitionSource));
  }

  getPromptInstructions(): string[] {
    return this.getDefinitions()
      .filter(t => t.promptInstructions)
      .map(t => `${t.name}: ${t.promptInstructions}`);
  }

  getExamplePrompts(): string[] {
    return this.getDefinitions().flatMap(t => t.examplePrompts ?? []);
  }

  has(name: string): boolean {
    return this.tools.has(name);
  }

  /** Returns schema rejections as tool results; only unknown tool names throw (specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md). */
  async execute(name: string, input: Record<string, unknown>, context?: ToolContext): Promise<ToolResponse> {
    const tool = this.tools.get(name);
    if (!tool) {
      log.warn('tool', 'tool not found', {name});
      throw new Error(`Unknown tool: ${name}`);
    }
    const definition = this.resolveDefinition(tool.definitionSource);
    const validate = this.compile(definition);
    if (!validate(input)) {
      const errors = validate.errors ?? [];
      const result = errors
        .map(error => {
          const details = error as unknown as {
            instancePath: string;
            dataPath?: string;
            schemaPath?: string;
            keyword: string;
            params: {missingProperty?: unknown; type?: unknown};
          };
          const schemaPath = details.schemaPath ?? '';
          const schemaProperties = [...schemaPath.matchAll(/\/properties\/([^/]+)/g)].map(match =>
            decodeJsonPointerPart(match[1])
          );
          const instancePath = resolveInstancePath(details.instancePath, details.dataPath, schemaProperties);
          const pathPrefix = instancePath && !instancePath.startsWith('/') ? `/${instancePath}` : instancePath;
          const path =
            `${pathPrefix}${isRequiredError(details.keyword) ? `/${String(details.params.missingProperty)}` : ''}` ||
            '/';
          if (isRequiredError(details.keyword)) return `${path} is required`;
          if (details.keyword === 'type') return `${path} must be ${String(details.params.type)}`;
          return `${path} failed ${details.keyword} validation`;
        })
        .join('; ');
      return {result};
    }
    log.info('tool', 'executing', {name, inputKeys: Object.keys(input)});
    const rawResult = await tool.execute(input, context);
    const response = normalizeToolResponse(rawResult);
    log.info('tool', 'execution complete', {
      name,
      rawType: typeof rawResult,
      clientMessageCount: response.clientMessages?.length ?? 0,
      clientMessageTypes: response.clientMessages?.map(m => m.type) ?? [],
      suppressAssistantResponse: response.suppressAssistantResponse ?? false,
    });
    return response;
  }
}
import {ToolRegistry} from './registry.js';
import Ajv from 'ajv';
import {jest} from '@jest/globals';

describe('ToolRegistry', () => {
  it('rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor', async () => {
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    const executor = jest.fn(async () => 'sunny');
    registry.register(weatherTool, executor);

    const response = await registry.execute('get_weather', {});

    expect(response.result).toMatch(/location.*required/i);
    expect(executor).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(0);
  });

  it('compiles a static schema once across ten executions', async () => {
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    const compile = jest.spyOn(Ajv.prototype, 'compile');
    registry.register(weatherTool, async () => 'sunny');

    for (let call = 0; call < 10; call += 1) {
      await registry.execute('get_weather', {location: 'Paris'});
    }

    expect(compile).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
    compile.mockRestore();
  });

  it('validates each function-valued definition against its current schema', async () => {
    let currentSchema = stringSchema;
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    const executor = jest.fn(async () => 'accepted');
    const compile = jest.spyOn(Ajv.prototype, 'compile');
    registry.register(() => ({...weatherTool, inputSchema: currentSchema}), executor);

    const first = await registry.execute('get_weather', {location: 'Paris'});
    await registry.execute('get_weather', {location: 'Berlin'});
    currentSchema = numberSchema;
    const second = await registry.execute('get_weather', {location: 'Paris'});

    expect({
      first: first.result,
      second: second.result,
    }).toEqual({
      first: 'accepted',
      second: expect.stringMatching(/\/location.*number/i),
    });
    expect(executor).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);
    expect(compile).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);
    compile.mockRestore();
  });

  it('passes valid input with undeclared properties through unchanged', async () => {
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    const input = {location: 'Paris', debugLabel: 'kept'};
    let receivedInput: Record<string, unknown> | undefined;
    const executor = jest.fn(async (received: Record<string, unknown>) => {
      receivedInput = received;
      return JSON.stringify(received);
    });
    registry.register(weatherTool, executor);

    await registry.execute('get_weather', input);

    expect(receivedInput).toEqual(input);
  });
});

const weatherTool = {
  name: 'get_weather',
  description: 'Get weather for a location',
  inputSchema: {
    type: 'object',
    properties: {location: {type: 'string'}},
    required: ['location'],
  },
};

const stringSchema = weatherTool.inputSchema;
const numberSchema = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {location: {type: 'number'}},
  required: ['location'],
};

const registryReturning = (response: ToolResponse): ToolRegistry => {
  const registry = new ToolRegistry();
  registry.register(
    {name: 'lookup', description: 'looks things up', inputSchema: {type: 'object'}},
    async () => response
  );
  return registry;
};

const TOOL_CALL: MessageChunk = {type: 'tool_use', toolCall: {id: 'call-1', name: 'lookup', input: {q: 'x'}}};
const STOP_FOR_TOOL: MessageChunk = {type: 'stop', stopReason: 'tool_use'};
const STOP_DONE: MessageChunk = {type: 'stop', stopReason: 'end_turn'};

const chunksFrom = async (stream: AsyncGenerator<MessageChunk>): Promise<MessageChunk[]> => {
  const chunks: MessageChunk[] = [];
  for await (const chunk of stream) chunks.push(chunk);
  return chunks;
};

describe('ChatOrchestrator tool loop', () => {
  it('returns schema rejections to the provider so it can correct a tool call', async () => {
    const requests: SendMessageParams[] = [];
    const inputSnapshots: unknown[] = [];
    const provider: AIProvider = {
      async *sendMessage(params: SendMessageParams): AsyncGenerator<MessageChunk> {
        requests.push(params);
        inputSnapshots.push(structuredClone(params.messages.at(-1)?.content));
        if (requests.length === 1) {
          yield {type: 'tool_use', toolCall: {id: 'bad-call', name: 'lookup', input: {}}};
          yield STOP_FOR_TOOL;
          return;
        }
        if (requests.length === 2) {
          yield {type: 'tool_use', toolCall: {id: 'good-call', name: 'lookup', input: {location: 'Paris'}}};
          yield STOP_FOR_TOOL;
          return;
        }
        yield {type: 'text', text: 'corrected'};
        yield STOP_DONE;
      },
      async generateStructured<T>(): Promise<T> {
        return {} as T;
      },
    };
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    let executorCalls = 0;
    const executor = async (): Promise<string> => {
      executorCalls += 1;
      return 'weather';
    };
    registry.register(
      {
        name: 'lookup',
        description: 'looks things up',
        inputSchema: {type: 'object', properties: {location: {type: 'string'}}, required: ['location']},
      },
      executor
    );
    const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(provider, promptBuilder, registry);

    const result = await orchestrator.processMessage(createSession('ask'));
    const secondRoundInput = inputSnapshots[1];

    expect({result, secondRoundInput, executorCalls}).toEqual({
      result: 'corrected',
      secondRoundInput: expect.arrayContaining([
        expect.objectContaining({type: 'tool_result', content: expect.stringMatching(/location.*required/i)}),
      ]),
      executorCalls: 1,
    });
  });

  it('runs another round after a tool call and streams both rounds in order', async () => {
    const provider = scriptedProvider([
      [TOOL_CALL, STOP_FOR_TOOL],
      [{type: 'text', text: 'the answer'}, STOP_DONE],
    ]);
    const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(provider, promptBuilder, registryReturning({result: 'found it'}));

    const chunks = await chunksFrom(orchestrator.processMessageStream(createSession('ask')));

    expect(chunks.map(c => c.type)).toEqual(['tool_use', 'stop', 'text', 'stop']);
  });

  it('stops after one round when nothing asked for a tool', async () => {
    const provider = scriptedProvider([[{type: 'text', text: 'done'}, STOP_DONE], [{type: 'text', text: 'never'}]]);
    const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(provider, promptBuilder, registryReturning({result: 'x'}));

    const text = await orchestrator.processMessage(createSession('ask'));

    expect(text).toBe('done');
  });

  it('stops asking for tools once maxToolRounds is spent', async () => {
    const alwaysTools = Array.from({length: 10}, () => [TOOL_CALL, STOP_FOR_TOOL]);
    const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(
      scriptedProvider(alwaysTools),
      promptBuilder,
      registryReturning({result: 'again'}),
      {maxToolRounds: 2}
    );

    const chunks = await chunksFrom(orchestrator.processMessageStream(createSession('ask')));

    expect(chunks.filter(c => c.type === 'tool_use')).toHaveLength(3);
  });

  it('forwards the client messages a tool returned as one tool_result chunk', async () => {
    const forwarded: OutgoingMessage = {type: 'entry_commit', index: 7};
    const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(
      scriptedProvider([[TOOL_CALL, STOP_FOR_TOOL], [STOP_DONE]]),
      promptBuilder,
      registryReturning({result: 'r', clientMessages: [forwarded]})
    );

    const chunks = await chunksFrom(orchestrator.processMessageStream(createSession('ask')));

    expect(chunks).toContainEqual({type: 'tool_result', clientMessages: [forwarded]});
  });

  it('appends an upserted entry to the session and rewrites its index to match', async () => {
    const entry: SessionEntry = {role: 'assistant', content: 'from the tool', timestamp: SENT_AT, isStreaming: false};
    const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(
      scriptedProvider([[TOOL_CALL, STOP_FOR_TOOL], [STOP_DONE]]),
      promptBuilder,
      registryReturning({result: 'r', clientMessages: [{type: 'entry_upsert', index: 999, entry}]})
    );
    const session = createSession('ask');

    const chunks = await chunksFrom(orchestrator.processMessageStream(session));

    expect(chunks).toContainEqual({
      type: 'tool_result',
      clientMessages: [{type: 'entry_upsert', index: session.entries.length - 1, entry}],
    });
  });

  it('asks for suppression when the tool says the reply is already handled', async () => {
    const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(
      scriptedProvider([[TOOL_CALL, STOP_FOR_TOOL], [STOP_DONE]]),
      promptBuilder,
      registryReturning({result: 'r', suppressAssistantResponse: true})
    );

    const chunks = await chunksFrom(orchestrator.processMessageStream(createSession('ask')));

    expect(chunks.map(c => c.type)).toEqual(['tool_use', 'stop', 'suppress_output', 'stop']);
  });

  it('joins the text of every round, not only the last', async () => {
    let seen = '';
    const hooks: OrchestratorHooks = {
      afterModelResponse: async (_session, responseText) => {
        seen = responseText;
      },
    };
    const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(
      scriptedProvider([
        [{type: 'text', text: 'first '}, TOOL_CALL, STOP_FOR_TOOL],
        [{type: 'text', text: 'second'}, STOP_DONE],
      ]),
      promptBuilder,
      registryReturning({result: 'r'}),
      {hooks}
    );

    await orchestrator.processMessage(createSession('ask'));

    expect(seen).toBe('first second');
  });

  it('keeps the usage an earlier round reported when a later round reports none', async () => {
    const usage: UsageMetadata = {inputTokens: 11, outputTokens: 3, totalTokens: 14};
    let seen: UsageMetadata | undefined;
    const hooks: OrchestratorHooks = {
      afterModelResponse: async (_session, _text, reported) => {
        seen = reported;
      },
    };
    const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(
      scriptedProvider([
        [TOOL_CALL, {type: 'stop', stopReason: 'tool_use', usage}],
        [{type: 'text', text: 'done'}, STOP_DONE],
      ]),
      promptBuilder,
      registryReturning({result: 'r'}),
      {hooks}
    );

